{
  "name": "Smart Customer Inquiry & Follow-Up Manager",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "note-overview",
      "name": "Read me — overview and setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -760,
        -520
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 760,
        "height": 300,
        "color": 2,
        "content": "## Smart Customer Inquiry & Follow-Up Manager\n### How it works\nA public n8n Form captures an inquiry. The workflow normalizes it, applies transparent priority rules, checks a Data Table for the same normalized email + subject + message within the configured window, stores only new inquiries, then optionally sends an internal SMTP alert. A schedule then checks stored, open records and sends limited internal reminders.\n\n### Setup\nCreate a Data Table named `customer_inquiries` with the columns in SETUP.md, then replace `REPLACE_WITH_DATA_TABLE_ID` in each Data Table node. Edit the clearly marked CONFIG object in **Normalize, validate & classify** and add an SMTP credential to the two email nodes. Set the workflow timezone, test with the Form Trigger test URL, then publish before using the production form URL.\n\n### Customization tips\nUse the Data Tables UI to change status safely. The default sends no customer email. Add bot protection at your website/proxy; n8n Form's Ignore Bots option is helpful but not a complete anti-abuse service."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note-intake",
      "name": "1 · Inquiry intake",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -760,
        -120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 350,
        "height": 120,
        "color": 0,
        "content": "## 1 · Start here: inquiry intake\nFor a test, open **Customer inquiry form** and click **Execute step**. Submit the test URL it opens. This upper path then stores and alerts. It is independent from the hourly reminder path below."
      }
    },
